WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:08.200
[MUSIC]

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:12.300
I think the impact of NLM globally is huge.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:17.300
We know that its collections, especially 
its online collections and resources

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:22.800
and tools are accessed by people all 
over the country and all over the world.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:27.900
It's there 24/7, 365, and it really makes 
a difference when somebody's undergoing...

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:31.300
when they're at that crisis moment, they
don't have time to go to the physical

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:35.800
library and spend hours researching or 
try to figure out where on the web has

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:39.000
valid health information. They know...
they can know this is a valid source--

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.000
it's been vetted properly--and it's 
really there for them.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:47.100
The impact is felt by everyone. 
Researchers all over the world use our

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:54.100
products, and by products I mean our 
databases, and so if we do something to

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:59.400
PubMed for example, we're gonna hear 
about it from people that are not only

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:04.700
in the United States but all over the 
world. And for a lot of these researchers,

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:11.700
PubMed is their first point of access to 
the medical literature because it's free.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:15.400
I would see it when I did reference just 
answering reference questions from all

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:20.300
over the world--from physicians, community 
organizations, the general public--

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:23.600
they come to us when they can go to their 
own medical libraries in their country--

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:25.800
they come to us, which is rather a 
compliment.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:30.400
We have a friend in Malaysia, and about 
five years ago his mother was diagnosed

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.100
with bladder cancer, and so he wrote 
to us and he was just sort of asking

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:38.800
for our support and I said, "You know, 
is there anything I can do to help you

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:43.200
get information about this, because you know, 
I know a great source for that, MedlinePlus.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.900
And he said that would be wonderful if 
you could provide some information.

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:50.100
So I did a quick search and I came across 
the MedlinePlus page on bladder cancer and

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.900
all the links to NCI bladder cancer 
resources and other resources that were

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:58.100
out there for him, and I sent those to him 
and about two or three months later

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:01.400
his mom had undergone some treatments 
and he wrote back and he said,

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:03.200
"I really wanna thank you,

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:08.400
because you provided more information 
to my family and I than her doctors did."

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:14.400
It is necessary to have one place that's 
reliable, that's...that does not have any

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:19.020
commercial pressures to represent what 
is the best known knowledge

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:23.000
in the field, and NLM offers that - worldwide.

